                <pb facs="0791" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg647"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Annex]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Legation to the
                            Department of State</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi></p>
                <p>Following are some further data on the administration of justice in China.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The Book of Obligations of the Civil Code has now been promulgated. The
                        remaining parts of the Civil Code as well as the Commercial Laws will be
                        promulgated very shortly according to latest reports.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>There are at present 1 Supreme Court, 28 High Courts (5 more than in
                        1926), 32 Branch High Courts (6 more than in 1926), 106 District Courts (40
                        more than 1926), and 207 Branch District Courts and Hsien Courts (184 more
                        than in 1926). The total number of new courts established since 1926 is 235,
                        an increase of 70 percent.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>There are at present 79 new prisons (16 more than in 1926).</item>
                </list>
            </div>
